# held/weapons/bow_self: the self bow in the fighter's LEFT hand (art weapon 3 with bowForm 1, `held bow.self`; the hunter's
# carried bow stays held/civil/bow, value `bow`), P2c SLICE-ARMS 2026-10-23. STYLE_P2 11 / 25.7-25.8: 23 px tip to tip, a
# 1 px stave of the person's wood stepped in runs of 4-3-2-1 to the curled tips (the upper limb lit, the lower a step
# darker, horn nocks), a leather wrap under the fist (the hand is drawn over it: P2C_CONTRACTS 4), the linen string 1 px.
# (LADDER-ARMS i1) facing D / U every string state is drawn at three-quarters (the owner, 2026-10-23: "too thin to
# read"): a 2 px stave at the grip (the wrap), the limbs curving over 4 columns to the nocks, the string 2 columns inside the grip (as before).
# Origin = the bow hand's gripL. Keys per facing x string state: carry (braced; INTEGRATE i1: was rest, so the LOCO frames leave it on the back), nock (the arrow on the string at the
# waist: a pixel of pull), draw (to the chest), full (to the cheek: the anchor), release (the string snapped straight with
# its blur a pixel either side: one frame), low (the drawn idle and walk: the bow low and tilted forward). The nocked arrow
# is the right hand's (arms/adult/action/twohand bow_r). Facing down the bow stands at screen right with the pull
# foreshortened; facing up at screen left, drawn over the body edge (LADDER-ARMS polish i1: was heldBack, so the bow vanished
# facing U); facing D / U the stave is edged dark both sides with its lit wood between (it read as a 1 px line). `drop` lies
# by a corpse's hand. Format: doll.h.
use person
legend V linen 0
legend W linen 1
legend X linen 2
legend Y linen 3
legend Z linen 4
body adult
role held bow.self
layer held
anchor gripL
keys held

